  "description": "Details of Condition 37 (Residential - Vertical sound transmission between potentially loud commercial and residential properties on new build) in respect of Site A / the Bromyard Site pursuant to planning permission 24/AP/2136 which gave consent for:\r\rVariation of Condition 1 Approved Plans pursuant to planning permission 22/AP/0554 (as amended by 23/AP/0953, 24/AP/2453 and 25/AP/0522), which gave consent for: The redevelopment of the Ledbury Estate involving the demolition of Bromyard House, Skenfrith House, Sarnsfield House and Peterchurch House and the erection of 6 blocks to provide 340 new homes (including 224 replacement homes), provision of Class E space fronting Old Kent Road at ground floor level, together with re-provision of the tenants and residents association hall and multi-use games area, access, servicing, car parking, cycle parking, cycle storage, plant, play and open space and landscaping.\r\rThe amendments include the following: \r- Amendments to introduce second staircases on Building B1 and B4 \r- Amendments to the wheelchair accessible dwelling strategy \r- Amendments to the Phase 2 landscape design \r- Amendments to Phase 2 cycle storage and servicing strategy on Buildings B1/B2/B3/B4 \r- Minor enhancements to external expression and materiality \r- Minor amendments to the elevations \r- Omission of roof top level plant screens",
